# Counter

The first Rocci app: one `.rocci` file, SQLite state, a page at `/`, and two
POST patches that morph `#counter`. Increment and reset each return the
`CounterCard` component. A second browser tab stays stale until you click or
reload. For two windows that share a stream, use the
[live counter](/examples/live-counter/).

This app is **docs-only** on rocci.dev. The home page already hosts a live
hybrid island counter; this page is the tutorial source.

Full file: [Counter.rocci](/examples/counter/source/Counter-rocci/).

## Run locally

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/counter/Counter.rocci
```

Pass `--no-window` to serve on [http://127.0.0.1:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000).
SQLite state is `examples/rocci/standalone/counter/counter.db` unless `DB_PATH`
is set.

## Smoke

```sh
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | grep -E 'datastar.js|id="counter"|Increment'
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/counter/increment
```

The POST returns a `datastar-patch-elements` event. For page chrome and
`@scope`, see [Styling](/examples/styling/).
